A gremlin stole my protection last night. (I didn't know, by the way, that 
they could do that; I knew they stole intrinsics, but I didn't know that 
bought protection counted.) I had had 5 or 6 points of protection, and it 
was all gone at one whack.

Okay, so I keep playing, and eventually get enough gold to donate again. But 
I'm a little glum about it; as I understood it, I've already used up my 
"initial donation" boost, so it's going to be one expensive point at a time. 
So I finally get back to a priest and donate. "Your devotion is rewarded." 
And suddenly, *all* the protection is back!

I had no idea the game operated that way. So, why? Does the game record 
whether or not you are protected as a boolean intrinsic, and the amount of 
your protection as an integer?

